---
description: Specifications governing check implementations
globs: headroom/checks/**/*.py,tests/test_checks_*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

- [spec/architecture/check-framework.md](mdc:spec/architecture/check-framework.md) -
  registry, the `BaseCheck` template, result categories.
- [spec/checks/index.md](mdc:spec/checks/index.md) - the inventory, the
  per-check document contract, and the unresolved-conflict table.
- [spec/contracts/results.md](mdc:spec/contracts/results.md) - for `base.py` and
  `registry.py`, which decide the shape every check writes.
- The check's own `spec/checks/scps/<name>.md` or `spec/checks/rcps/<name>.md`.
  An RCP check also needs [spec/contracts/policy-model.md](mdc:spec/contracts/policy-model.md).

A new check needs its specification before its code.
`tests/test_spec_corpus.py` fails until it exists.
[HOW_TO_ADD_A_CHECK.md](mdc:HOW_TO_ADD_A_CHECK.md) is the authoring runbook.
